 # lakeside-desk
 
+Version: 1 · Updated: 2026-10-27
+
 The Lakeside Windsurf School teaches windsurfing on the lake from April to October, and rents boards and
 sails to its students and to visitors who bring their own experience. This repository holds the software
 of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
+
+## Rental service
+
+`createRentalService()` is exported from `src/index.ts`. Each instance owns an independent in-memory
+inventory and booking calendar; its data is lost when the instance is discarded.
+
+```ts
+import { createRentalService } from './src/index.js';
+
+const rentals = createRentalService();
+rentals.addEquipment({ id: 'board-1', kind: 'board', dailyPrice: 2500 });
+
+const request = {
+  itemId: 'board-1',
+  start: '2026-06-01T00:00:00Z',
+  end: '2026-06-04T00:00:00Z',
+};
+rentals.quote(request); // { ...request, total: 7500 }
+rentals.book(request); // { id: 'booking-1', ...request, total: 7500 }
+```
+
+- `addEquipment(item)` registers a board or sail. Duplicate IDs and invalid equipment throw errors.
+- `quote(request)` returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }` without reserving equipment. A quote does
+  not check availability, so already-booked periods can still be priced.
+- `book(request)` returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }` and reserves the whole period. Booking
+  IDs are sequential within each instance. Failed bookings do not consume an ID.
+
+Prices and totals are nonnegative, safe integer numbers of euro cents. Totals equal the daily price
+multiplied by the number of days; an unrepresentable total throws an error.
+
+Times use ISO-8601 extended calendar timestamps at midnight UTC, with `Z` or `+00:00`. Seconds may be
+omitted, and fractional seconds must be all zero. Calendar dates must exist. Returned timestamps
+preserve the supplied strings. A rental includes its start and excludes its end: June 1 through June 3
+ends at midnight on June 4. The end must be after the start. Both operations reject unknown equipment
+and invalid periods. An item cannot have overlapping bookings, but adjacent periods are allowed.
+
+Cancellation is deferred. The school's policy for a future cancellation feature is: less than 24 hours
+before the start, no refund; otherwise, refund the full amount. Exactly 24 hours qualifies for a full
+refund. All policy times are UTC.
+
+## Development
+
+Run `npm ci` to install development tools, `npm run build` to compile TypeScript and declarations to
+`dist/`, and `npm test` to build and run the deterministic rental tests with Node's test runner.
