index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0a27443b02634ebc1de79e39a6a7516a73712170
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-001-use-sequential-booking-identifiers.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-use-sequential-booking-identifiers
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use sequential booking identifiers"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The initial rental service must return an identifier for each booking, while keeping all state in
+memory. The service must be deterministic and must not use a clock or random value to create IDs.
+
+## Decision
+
+Assign booking IDs sequentially within each service instance, using the `booking-<number>` format,
+starting at `booking-1`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Booking IDs are predictable and unique for the lifetime of a service instance. They reset when a
+new in-memory service is created, which is appropriate until persistence is introduced.
