@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+---
+id: task-001-implement-in-memory-rental-service
+type: task
+title: "Implement in-memory rental service"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+version: 1
+date: 2026-10-27
+---
+
+Implemented the initial in-memory rental module exported from `src/index.ts`.
+
+The module validates equipment and UTC whole-day rental periods, calculates safe integer-cent totals,
+and prevents overlapping bookings for an item. It uses sequential booking identifiers as approved in
+`../decision-log/dl-001-use-sequential-booking-identifiers.md`. Caller-owned inputs and returned objects
+cannot mutate stored inventory or reservations. Each instance owns its own state.
+
+Added public API documentation and usage examples to `README.md`, including the school's deferred
+cancellation policy: no refund less than 24 hours before the start, full refund otherwise. No
+cancellation API was implemented.
+
+Added TypeScript as a development-only dependency, a build command, and deterministic tests using
+Node's built-in test runner. There are no runtime dependencies.
+
+## Verification
+
+All acceptance criteria concern new behavior and use red-first testing rather than characterization.
+The first test execution failed because the rental module did not yet exist. After implementation,
+`npm test` passes all 11 tests and strict TypeScript compilation. Tests cover equipment validation,
+unknown items, integer cents and overflow, UTC midnight and calendar validation, leap days, pricing,
+booking IDs, every overlap shape, adjacent bookings, and state isolation. Installing development
+dependencies reported no known vulnerabilities.
